 "text": "Hey, nice to hear from you. How are you? Stairs are tricky. Is he able to climb stairs bit at a time, or does he need a stair lift? Then I'd show him. A lift means he can see the whole flat without effort, while climbing bit at a time lets him feel more in control. Yes, a chair on the landing is the simplest and safest way up and down. You could also get a tiny folding ladder and borrow a friend's help to set it up. Keep the flat clear so he can see where he's going. That's the kindest thing. Your granddad will be touched you made the effort.",
